    <p class="section-label">Gear</p>
    <h1 class="about-intro__headline">
      The tools and hardware I use to do my best work
    </h1>
    <div class="about-intro__body">
      <div class="prose">

        <h2>Hardware</h2>

        <h3>Computer</h3>
        <p>I work on a <strong>MacBook Pro 14"</strong> (M1 Max) paired with a BenQ 4K 32 Inch monitor at my desk. The combination of portability and power covers everything from heavy Figma files to light development work.</p>

        <h3>Peripherals</h3>
        <p>I use an <strong>Apple Magic Keyboard with Touch ID</strong> and a <strong>Logitech MX Master 3</strong> mouse. For longer sessions I switch to a <strong>Keychron K2 Pro</strong> mechanical keyboard with Gateron brown switches.</p>

        <h3>Tablet</h3>
        <p>A <strong>Wacom Intuus Pro (Medium)</strong> lives on my desk for detailed illustration and photo retouching work. For sketching away from the desk I use an <strong>iPad Pro 11"</strong> with the Apple Pencil.</p>

        <h2>Design Software</h2>

        <h3>Figma</h3>
        <p>Figma is my primary design and prototyping tool. I use it for everything from early wireframes to high-fidelity component libraries and interactive prototypes.</p>


        <h3>Adobe Creative Suite</h3>
        <p>I keep a Creative Cloud subscription primarily for Photoshop (photo editing and compositing) and Illustrator (vector illustration and icon work).</p>

        <h2>Development Tools</h2>

        <h3>IDE / Editor</h3>
        <p>Visual Studio Code is my current editor of choice. I keep the theme minimal — currently running the default dark high contrast theme — and rely on a small set of extensions: Claude Code, Live Server, Figma, and Nunjucks language support.</p>

        <h3>Terminal</h3>
        <p>I use the <a href="https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/">Kitty</a> Terminal app with <strong>zsh</strong> and <a href="https://ohmyz.sh/">Oh My Zsh</a>. Nothing fancy — I find a clean, fast terminal more useful than a heavily configured one.</p>

        <h3>Version Control</h3>
        <p>Git from the command line for most things, with the GitHub desktop app occasionally for quick visual diffs on larger PRs.</p>

        <h2>Productivity</h2>

        <h3>Note-taking</h3>
        <p><strong>Obsidian</strong> for long-form notes, research, and design documentation. <strong>Apple Notes</strong> for quick capture and anything shared across devices.</p>

        <h3>Task Management</h3>
        <p>I keep task management simple — a combination of <strong>Things 3</strong> for personal project tracking and whatever tool the team is using at work (currently Linear).</p>

        <h3>Communication</h3>
        <p>Slack for work, iMessage and Signal for personal. I keep notifications aggressively managed and batch async communication rather than staying always-on.</p>

        <h2>This Site</h2>

        <p>This site is built with <a href="https://www.11ty.dev/">11ty</a>, styled with modern CSS using cascade layers and container queries, and deployed to <a href="https://www.netlify.com/">Netlify</a>. Source code is on <a href="https://github.com/pdkaizer">GitHub</a>.</p>

      </div>
